Before I post the Call for Votes for the rec.games.roguelike.* groups, I
need to determine what change should be proposed for rec.games.rogue.

The second RFD contained proposals 1 and 2, and two versions of proposal 3.

Proposal 1: Move rec.games.hack to rec.games.roguelike.nethack.
Proposal 2: Move rec.games.moria to rec.games.roguelike.moria.

Proposal 3A: Move rec.games.rogue to rec.games.roguelike.rogue.
Proposal 3B: Move rec.games.rogue to the existing group 
rec.games.roguelike.misc.

Much of the discussion has focused on the desirability of the
reorganization as a whole; this has made it difficult for me to
determine the actual consensus for the Rogue group.  Therefore, I am
conducting a straw poll, to get opinions on this issue.  (Thanks to Per
Abrahamsen for suggesting the poll.)

I am treating this as an advisory poll, not a strict vote; for example,
if there is a slight preference for proposal 3A in terms of total votes,
but the voters who show a strong preference clearly prefer 3B, then 3B
may be on the ballot.

--Delete everything above this line when replying--
1. Do you prefer proposal 3A (moving the Rogue group to
rec.games.roguelike.rogue) or 3B (moving it into the existing
rec.games.roguleike.misc)?

2. Do you intend to vote differently on the proposals?  If so, how?
(Example: "I will abstain from 3A but vote against 3B.")

3. Will your votes on the other proposals depend on which version of
proposal 3 is on the ballot?  If so, how?

4. Do you read rec.games.rogue now?

5. Any comments?

